   "claims": [
    "For example, if your step length is 2.4′ and you walked 9,500 steps in a day, that would equal 22,800, which would be your distance in feet.",
    "To convert the distance to miles, divide the final distance by 5,280 (the number of feet in a mile).",
    "For example, a person who is 70″ tall with a stride of 31 1/2” (a step length of 2.62′) and walked 10,000 steps will have walked a distance of 315,000″.",
    "For most people, walking 10,000 steps is approximately five miles.[5] With that said, factors such as the intensity level of your walk as well as your stride length will determine exactly how far you walk.",
    "As we just mentioned, your stride length and walking intensity will affect the exact distance you walk per step, but most people will walk around 10 miles in 20,000 steps.",
    "An elite runner can run a mile in under 5 minutes, but most people run a mile in 6-13 minutes.[7] Steps to Miles Chart The chart below shows the average distance walked for various step-counts."
   ],
